 "pattern": "Binary search over a flattened matrix",
 "statement": "Each row of `matrix` is sorted from left to right, and the first number of each row is larger than the last number of the row above. Return `True` if `target` is in the matrix. The solution must run in O(log(m · n)) time.",
 "example": {
  "input": "matrix = [[1,3,5,7],[10,11,16,20],[23,30,34,60]], target = 16",
  "output": "True",
  "why": "16 is in row 1, column 2."
 },
 "more": [
